 "title_en": "Funny Stories from Life (7/20): Buying the Wrong Soy Sauce Three Times",
 "free": false,
 "audio_url": null,
 "note_en": "生抽 (light soy sauce, for flavour) and 老抽 (dark soy sauce, for colour) are easy to mix up if you don't read the label. \"Fridge blindness\" (冰箱失明症) is a real internet phrase for staring right at the thing you need without seeing it. 耙耳朵 (\"soft ears\") is the Sichuan nickname for caring husbands who cook and spoil their wives, a real stereotype that runs opposite to the Western image of the man in the kitchen. Dongpo pork (东坡肉) and Kung Pao chicken (宫保鸡丁) are said to be named after real officials, Su Dongpo and Ding Baozhen.",
 "series": "funnytales",
